    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d726">

                <pb facs="0760" n="756" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg756"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/6902: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-06-03T15:00:00+01:00">June 3, 1939—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 3—1:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1061. Your 396, June 2, 7 p.m., was taken up this morning with the Chief of the
                    Far Eastern Division at the Foreign Office.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d726-f1"/> He
                    said that on May 24 the Foreign Office had transmitted to the Ministry of
                    Colonies the request of the Chinese Ambassador for facilities for the transit of
                    these tung oil shipments. Chauvel stated that he would at once get in touch with
                    the Minister of Colonies, explain the considerations set out in your telegram
                    and urge that for these reasons the Chinese Ambassador’s request should be
                    granted without delay.<anchor n="66" xml:id="d726-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d726-f1" n="65" xml:id="d726-f1-content">
                <p>Jean Chauvel.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d726-f2" n="66" xml:id="d726-f2-content">
                <p>The Ambassador in France took up the question again on June 6.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
